TO KEEP THE JOB RUNNING

Run `ssoossh service enroll` again on the host that holds the key, and have
the new request approved. That mints a new code; the old one keeps working
until it expires, so there is no gap if you do it before the date above.

Certificates already issued from this code are unaffected. They stay valid
for their own lifetimes, which is why a job can keep running for a while
after the code behind it has expired.
